macro_rules! d_RecordBasis_3c4e3c32 {
    () => {
        "\"RecordBasis\":{\"description\":\"What kind of claim a record is, as its author states it. OPTIONAL wherever it appears; absent means the author did not say, and a reader shows it as unstated rather than assuming any of these.\\n\\n  - `declared` — the author's own statement: a decision, a preference, an intention, a commitment. True because the author says so, and only as far as the author speaks for it.\\n  - `observed` — something the author saw, measured or was told directly, recorded as found.\\n  - `verified` — checked against evidence that somebody else can check again, such as a credential or another record. A record that says `verified` SHOULD name that evidence in `evidence`; one that does not is an unsupported claim to have checked, and a reader SHOULD present it so.\\n  - `inferred` — derived by reasoning from other information: an agent's conclusion, a summary's generalisation, a model's guess. The value an agent writer uses when it does not know which of the others applies.\\n\\nThe values are the author's account of their own record, signed with it. They are not checked by anybody, confer nothing, and say nothing about whether the record is right — `inferred` can be correct and `observed` mistaken. Aligned with the provenance vocabulary of personal agent memory, so that a record moved between a member's memory and a room keeps its meaning.\",\"enum\":[\"declared\",\"observed\",\"verified\",\"inferred\"],\"title\":\"RecordBasis\",\"type\":\"string\"}"
    };
}
pub(crate) use d_RecordBasis_3c4e3c32;

