macro_rules! d_SignAlgorithm_586d14d0 {
    () => {
        "\"SignAlgorithm\":{\"description\":\"`EdDSA` pairs with an `ed25519` key; `ES256` pairs with a `p256` key; `ML-DSA-44` and `ML-DSA-65` pair with `mldsa44` and `mldsa65` keys respectively. An `x25519` key performs key agreement and can sign nothing, so no algorithm here is valid for one. These are JOSE algorithm identifiers, externally owned, so they are carried verbatim and never re-cased (SPEC.md §4.10 rule 5); the ML-DSA names are those RFC 9964 registers in the JOSE Web Signature and Encryption Algorithms registry, which is why their hyphenated casing differs from the `keyType` values beside them — those are specification-defined. The set is expected to grow as algorithms are registered. The enumeration remains closed: an unrecognised algorithm is refused rather than silently substituted with a supported one.\",\"enum\":[\"EdDSA\",\"ES256\",\"ML-DSA-44\",\"ML-DSA-65\"],\"title\":\"SignAlgorithm\",\"type\":\"string\"}"
    };
}
pub(crate) use d_SignAlgorithm_586d14d0;

macro_rules! d_SignalDelay_d311c858 {
    () => {
        "\"SignalDelay\":{\"description\":\"Whether a room's host waits a randomised interval before sending a `rooms/changed` signal: the room's **signal delay**.\\n\\n`randomised` is the default and what a room without one has: the host waits a few seconds after the change that fires a watch, so that the signal's time does not mark one write exactly (`rooms/changed`, producer item 4). `none` is for a room where members expect to see a write as soon as it is made, such as a conversation: the host sends the signal as soon as the change that fires it is stored, with no wait of its own.\\n\\n**A room's setting, not a member's.** The delay protects the room's writers as much as its watchers. A watcher whose signal is sent at once marks, to anyone who sees both the writer's request reach the host and the signal leave it, the moment of the write and that the two parties share the room. So one watcher cannot opt out for itself without giving away something about everyone who writes, and the setting is the room's: changed by a holder of `admin` (`rooms/signal-delay/set`) and served to every member (`rooms/info`).\\n\\n**What `none` gives up.** Little in a busy room, where writes are frequent enough that their rhythm is visible anyway; most in a quiet one, where a single write and a single signal line up. A surface that offers the setting SHOULD say so.\\n\\nAbsent means `randomised`.\",\"enum\":[\"randomised\",\"none\"],\"title\":\"SignalDelay\",\"type\":\"string\"}"
    };
}
pub(crate) use d_SignalDelay_d311c858;

